IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 2, regulations 100 to 105: sanctions, and how long a reduction
-- in the amount of an award lasts.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. Whether a failure is sanctionable, and whether the Secretary of State has decided to reduce an award, are stated BOOLEAN
-- inputs. The rules say how long a reduction lasts on the facts given; nothing here imposes a sanction.
--
-- NOT COVERED. A cell of a table marked "–" gives no answer for that combination, and a cell marked "..." is blank in this text.
-- A rule that reaches one returns NOTHING. So does a rule that is asked about a claimant under 16, because no table has a column for one.
--
-- "WITHIN 365 DAYS BEGINNING WITH THE DATE OF THE CURRENT FAILURE". The tables ask whether the date of the most recent PREVIOUS failure
-- is within a stretch of days beginning with the date of the CURRENT failure. A previous failure lies before the current one, so read
-- forward the stretch can never hold it, and every claimant would get the first-offence row. The rules read the stretch backward,
-- as the days ending with the date of the current failure, both ends counted: within 365 days is a gap of 0 to 364 days,
-- and within 14 days is a gap of 0 to 13 days (fork F-102-1).

§ `Chapter 2 — Sanctions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 100 — Introduction`

-- Paragraph (1): this Chapter is about the reduction in an award in the event of a failure sanctionable under section 26 or 27 of the Act
-- ("a sanctionable failure").
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- src:1594 | CHAPTER 2 — SANCTIONS
-- src:1595 | 100 Introduction
-- src:1596 | (1) This Chapter contains provisions about the reduction in the amount of an award of universal credit in the event of a failure by a claimant which is sanctionable under section 26 or 27 of the Act (“a sanctionable failure”).
@ref reg 100(1) (src:1594-1596)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 100(1) — a sanctionable failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` MEANS
    `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` OR `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act`

-- Paragraph (1A): a "current sanctionable failure" is a sanctionable failure in relation to which the Secretary of State has not yet
-- determined whether the amount of an award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- src:1597 | (1A) In this Chapter references to a “current sanctionable failure” are to a sanctionable failure in relation to which the Secretary of State has not yet determined whether the amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
@ref reg 100(1A) (src:1597)
GIVEN `the failure is a sanctionable failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has determined whether the amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act in relation to the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 100(1A) — a current sanctionable failure` `the failure is a sanctionable failure` `the Secretary of State has determined whether the amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act in relation to the failure` MEANS
    `the failure is a sanctionable failure`
    AND (NOT `the Secretary of State has determined whether the amount of an award of universal credit is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act in relation to the failure`)

-- Paragraphs (2) to (5) say where in the Chapter each matter is dealt with. They state no rule and have no rule in this module
-- (coverage row: inert, a pure citation).
-- src:1598 | (2) How the period of the reduction for each sanctionable failure is to be determined is dealt with in regulations 101 to 105.
-- src:1599 | (3) When the reduction begins or ceases to have effect is dealt with in regulations 106 to 109.
-- src:1600 | (4) How the amount of a reduction is calculated for an assessment period in which the reduction has effect is set out in regulations 110 and 111.
-- src:1601 | (5) Regulations 112 to 114 provide for some miscellaneous matters (movement of sanctions from a jobseeker's allowance or an employment and support allowance, cases in which no reduction is made for a sanctionable failure and prescription of work placement scheme for the purposes of section 26(2)(a) of the Act).
@ref reg 100(2) to (5) (src:1598-1601)
`reg 100(2) to (5) — where the Chapter deals with the period of a reduction, when it takes effect, how much it is, and some other matters` MEANS
        "Regulations 101 to 105 determine the period of a reduction, regulations 106 to 109 when it begins or ceases to have effect, regulations 110 and 111 its amount, and regulations 112 to 114 some miscellaneous matters."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 101 — General principles for calculating reduction periods`

-- Paragraph (1): the reduction period for each sanctionable failure is determined under regulations 102 to 105, subject to paragraphs (3)
-- and (4). The rules for those regulations are below, and the seat layer picks the one that applies (coverage row: inert, a pure citation).
-- src:1602 | Reduction periods
-- src:1603 | 101 General principles for calculating reduction periods
-- src:1604 | (1) The number of days for which a reduction in the amount of an award is to have effect (“the reduction period”) is to be determined in relation to each sanctionable failure in accordance with regulations 102 to 105, but subject to paragraphs (3) and (4).
@ref reg 101(1) (src:1602-1604)
`reg 101(1) — the reduction period for each sanctionable failure is determined under regulations 102 to 105` MEANS
        "The number of days for which a reduction in the amount of an award is to have effect (the reduction period) is determined for each sanctionable failure under regulations 102 to 105, subject to paragraph (3) and (4)."

-- Paragraph (2): reduction periods run consecutively. A further period can begin only on the day after the one before it ends
-- (fork F-101-1: "consecutively" is read as one directly after another, with no gap and no overlap).
-- src:1605 | (2) Reduction periods are to run consecutively.
@ref reg 101(2) (src:1605)
GIVEN `the last day of the reduction period before` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 101(2) — the first day on which the next reduction period can run` `the last day of the reduction period before` MEANS
    `the last day of the reduction period before` PLUS 1

-- Paragraph (5): "the total outstanding reduction period" is the total number of days for which no reduction in an award under section 26 or 27
-- has yet been applied.
-- src:1608 | (5) In paragraph (3) “the total outstanding reduction period” is the total number of days for which no reduction in an award under section 26 or 27 of the Act has yet been applied.
@ref reg 101(5) (src:1608)
GIVEN `number of days of each reduction period for which no reduction has yet been applied` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 101(5) — the total outstanding reduction period` `number of days of each reduction period for which no reduction has yet been applied` MEANS
    sum `number of days of each reduction period for which no reduction has yet been applied`

-- Paragraph (3): if the reduction period calculated under regulations 102 to 105 would result in the total outstanding reduction period
-- exceeding 1095 days, the reduction period is adjusted so that the total does not exceed 1095 days. The total of the earlier days is the
-- input; the new period is cut to what remains of the 1095, and to nothing if no days remain (fork F-101-2).
-- src:1606 | (3) If the reduction period calculated in relation to a sanctionable failure in accordance with regulations 102 to 105 would result in the total outstanding reduction period exceeding 1095 days, the reduction period in relation to that failure is to be adjusted so that the total outstanding reduction period does not exceed 1095 days.
@ref reg 101(3) (src:1606)
GIVEN `reduction period calculated in accordance with regulations 102 to 105` IS A NUMBER
      `total outstanding reduction period before this failure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 101(3) — the reduction period adjusted so that the total outstanding reduction period does not exceed 1095 days` `reduction period calculated in accordance with regulations 102 to 105` `total outstanding reduction period before this failure` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, minimum (LIST `reduction period calculated in accordance with regulations 102 to 105`, 1095 MINUS `total outstanding reduction period before this failure`))

-- Paragraph (4) is a run of dots in this text (coverage row: repealed or blank in this text).
-- src:1607 | (4) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref reg 101(4) (src:1607)
`reg 101(4) — a run of dots in the text, not encoded` MEANS "(4) . . . ."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The shared parts of the three tables`

-- The tables in regulations 102(2), 103(2) and 104(2)(b) ask the same two questions of the claimant's earlier failures. First, which is
-- the most recent previous sanctionable failure (of the kind the regulation counts), how long ago was it, and what reduction period applied
-- to it. The record below holds those facts of one earlier failure; the caller says, for each, whether it gave rise to a higher-level sanction,
-- whether it falls within regulation 103(1), and whether it falls within regulation 104(1).
-- src:1609 | 102 Higher-level sanction
-- src:1610 | (1) This regulation specifies the reduction period for a sanctionable failure under section 26 of the Act (“higher level sanction”).
-- src:1611 | (2) Where the sanctionable failure is not a pre-claim failure, the reduction in the circumstances described in the first column of the following table is the period set out in—
-- src:1612 | (a) the second column, where the claimant is aged 18 or over on the date of the sanctionable failure;
-- src:1613 | (b) the third column, where the claimant is aged 16 or 17 on the date of the sanctionable failure.
-- src:1614 | | Circumstances in which reduction period applies | Reduction period where claimant aged 18 or over | Reduction period where claimant aged 16 or 17 |
-- src:1615 | | Where there has been no previous sanctionable failure by the claimant giving rise to a higher-level sanction | 91 days | 14 days |
-- src:1616 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant giving rise to a higher-level sanction and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is not within 365 days beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure | 91 days | 14 days |
-- src:1617 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant giving rise to a higher-level sanction and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is within 365 days, but not within 14 days, beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure and the reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure is— | | |
-- src:1618 | | (a) 14 days | – | 28 days |
-- src:1619 | | (b) 28 days | – | 28 days |
-- src:1620 | | (c) 91 days | 182 days | – |
-- src:1621 | | (d) 182 days | 182 days | – |
-- src:1622 | | (e) ... | . . . | – |
-- src:1623 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant giving rise to a higher-level sanction and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is within 14 days beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure and the reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure is— | | |
-- src:1624 | | (a) 14 days | – | 14 days |
-- src:1625 | | (b) 28 days | – | 28 days |
-- src:1626 | | (c) 91 days | 91 days | – |
-- src:1627 | | (d) 182 days | 182 days | – |
-- src:1628 | | (e) ... | . . . | – |
@ref reg 102(2) (the previous failures) (src:1609-1628)
DECLARE `Previous sanctionable failure` HAS
    `date of the previous sanctionable failure`                                    IS A DATE
    `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days`   IS A NUMBER
    `the previous sanctionable failure was a pre-claim failure`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous sanctionable failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 103(1)`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)`             IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Age band for a reduction period` IS ONE OF
    `aged 18 or over`
    `aged 16 or 17`

DECLARE `Recency of the most recent previous sanctionable failure` IS ONE OF
    `no previous sanctionable failure`
    `previous failure not within 365 days`
    `previous failure within 365 days but not within 14 days`
    `previous failure within 14 days`

-- The age band: 18 or over, or 16 or 17, on the date of the sanctionable failure. No table has a column for anyone under 16.
@ref reg 102(2) (src:1612-1613)
GIVEN `age of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Age band for a reduction period`
`reg 102(2) — the age band of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` `age of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` MEANS
    IF `age of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` AT LEAST 18
    THEN JUST `aged 18 or over`
    ELSE IF `age of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` AT LEAST 16
         THEN JUST `aged 16 or 17`
         ELSE NOTHING

-- The most recent of some earlier failures: the one with the latest date. Two earlier failures on the same day are not told apart by the
-- text; the first one given is taken.
@ref reg 102(2) (src:1615-1617)
GIVEN failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Previous sanctionable failure`
`reg 102(2) — the most recent of some previous sanctionable failures` failures MEANS
    CONSIDER failures
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER filter (GIVEN f YIELD (Day (f's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) EQUALS `latest day`) (first FOLLOWED BY rest)
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN latest FOLLOWED BY others THEN JUST latest
        WHERE
            `latest day` MEANS maximum (map (GIVEN f YIELD Day (f's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) (first FOLLOWED BY rest))

-- How recent is the most recent previous failure, counted back from the current failure with both ends counted (fork F-102-1).
-- A previous failure dated after the current one is not "previous": NOTHING.
@ref reg 102(2) (src:1616-1617)
GIVEN `date of the current sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      previous IS A MAYBE `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Recency of the most recent previous sanctionable failure`
`reg 102(2) — how recent the most recent previous sanctionable failure is` `date of the current sanctionable failure` previous MEANS
    CONSIDER previous
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `no previous sanctionable failure`
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        IF (Day `date of the current sanctionable failure` MINUS Day (p's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) LESS THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF (Day `date of the current sanctionable failure` MINUS Day (p's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) AT LEAST 365
             THEN JUST `previous failure not within 365 days`
             ELSE IF (Day `date of the current sanctionable failure` MINUS Day (p's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) AT LEAST 14
                  THEN JUST `previous failure within 365 days but not within 14 days`
                  ELSE JUST `previous failure within 14 days`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 102 — Higher-level sanction`

-- Paragraph (1): this regulation specifies the reduction period for a sanctionable failure under section 26 of the Act. Paragraph (5):
-- "higher-level sanction" means a sanction under section 26, and "pre-claim failure" means a failure sanctionable under section 26(4).
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 102(1) (src:1610)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 102(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` MEANS
    `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act`

-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- src:1634 | (5) In this regulation—
-- src:1635 | “higher-level sanction” means a sanction under section 26 of the Act;
-- src:1636 | “pre-claim failure” means a failure sanctionable under section 26(4) of the Act.
@ref reg 102(5) (src:1634-1636)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 26(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 102(5) — a pre-claim failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 26(4) of the Act` MEANS
    `the failure is sanctionable under section 26(4) of the Act`

-- Paragraph (3): where the other failure referred to in paragraph (2) was a pre-claim failure it is disregarded in determining the
-- reduction period. The most recent failure that counts is therefore the most recent one that gave rise to a higher-level sanction and was
-- not a pre-claim failure (fork F-102-2: "disregarded" means the next most recent failure then counts).
-- src:1629 | (3) But where the other sanctionable failure referred to in paragraph (2) was a pre-claim failure it is disregarded in determining the reduction period in accordance with that paragraph.
@ref reg 102(3) (src:1629)
GIVEN failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Previous sanctionable failure`
`reg 102(3) — the most recent previous sanctionable failure giving rise to a higher-level sanction, disregarding a pre-claim failure` failures MEANS
    `reg 102(2) — the most recent of some previous sanctionable failures`
        (filter (GIVEN f YIELD (f's `the previous sanctionable failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction`) AND (NOT (f's `the previous sanctionable failure was a pre-claim failure`))) failures)

-- Paragraph (2): the reduction period, for a failure that is not a pre-claim failure, from the table. The first column gives the
-- circumstances; the second the period for a claimant aged 18 or over on the date of the failure; the third for one aged 16 or 17.
-- A cell marked "–" is not answered: NOTHING. The rows marked (e) are blank in this text ("..."): NOTHING for any period that is not
-- in rows (a) to (d).
@ref reg 102(2) (src:1611-1628)
GIVEN band IS AN `Age band for a reduction period`
      recency IS A `Recency of the most recent previous sanctionable failure`
      `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 102(2) — the reduction period in the table` band recency `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` MEANS
    CONSIDER recency
    WHEN `no previous sanctionable failure` THEN `no previous failure, or one not within 365 days`
    WHEN `previous failure not within 365 days` THEN `no previous failure, or one not within 365 days`
    WHEN `previous failure within 365 days but not within 14 days` THEN `within 365 days but not within 14 days`
    WHEN `previous failure within 14 days` THEN `within 14 days`
    WHERE
        `no previous failure, or one not within 365 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER band
            WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN JUST 91
            WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN JUST 14
        `within 365 days but not within 14 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER band
            WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 91 THEN JUST 182
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 182 THEN JUST 182
                     ELSE NOTHING
            WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 28
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 28
                     ELSE NOTHING
        `within 14 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER band
            WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 91 THEN JUST 91
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 182 THEN JUST 182
                     ELSE NOTHING
            WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 14
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 28
                     ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 102(2) (src:1611-1613)
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `date of the current sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 102(2) — the reduction period for a sanctionable failure that is not a pre-claim failure` age `date of the current sanctionable failure` failures MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — the age band of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` age
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST band THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — how recent the most recent previous sanctionable failure is` `date of the current sanctionable failure` `the previous failure that counts`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST recency THEN `reg 102(2) — the reduction period in the table` band recency `the period of the previous failure`
    WHERE
        `the previous failure that counts` MEANS `reg 102(3) — the most recent previous sanctionable failure giving rise to a higher-level sanction, disregarding a pre-claim failure` failures
        `the period of the previous failure` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the previous failure that counts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST p THEN p's `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days`

-- Paragraph (4): where the failure is a pre-claim failure, the period is the lesser of (a) the period that would apply under paragraph (2)
-- if it were not a pre-claim failure, and (b) where the failure relates to paid work due to last for a limited period, the days beginning
-- with the day after the failure and ending with the date on which the limited period would have ended, MINUS the number of days beginning
-- with the day after the failure and ending on the day before the date of claim. The "minus" closes the whole sentence, outside both limbs,
-- and is read as applying to the lesser of the two (fork F-102-3). The result can be negative or zero; regulation 113(1)(e) deals with that.
-- A claim made on or before the failure leaves no days to take away, so none are taken.
-- src:1630 | (4) Where the sanctionable failure for which a reduction period is to be determined is a pre-claim failure, the period is the lesser of—
-- src:1631 | (a) the period that would be applicable to the claimant under paragraph (2) if it were not a pre-claim failure; or
-- src:1632 | (b) where the sanctionable failure relates to paid work that was due to last for a limited period, the period beginning with the day after the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with the date on which the limited period would have ended,
-- src:1633 | minus the number of days beginning with the day after the date of the sanctionable failure and ending on the day before the date of claim.
@ref reg 102(4) (src:1630-1633)
GIVEN `the period that would be applicable under paragraph (2) if the failure were not a pre-claim failure` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `date of the sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `date on which the limited period would have ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date of claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 102(4) — the reduction period for a pre-claim failure` `the period that would be applicable under paragraph (2) if the failure were not a pre-claim failure` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the limited period would have ended` `date of claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period that would be applicable under paragraph (2) if the failure were not a pre-claim failure`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (`the lesser of (a) and (b)` a MINUS `the days from the day after the failure to the day before the date of claim`)
    WHERE
        `the lesser of (a) and (b)` a MEANS
            CONSIDER `date on which the limited period would have ended`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN a
            WHEN JUST ends THEN minimum (LIST a, Day ends MINUS Day `date of the sanctionable failure`)
        `the days from the day after the failure to the day before the date of claim` MEANS
            maximum (LIST 0, (Day `date of claim` MINUS Day `date of the sanctionable failure`) MINUS 1)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 103 — Medium-level sanction`

-- Paragraph (1): this regulation specifies the reduction period for a failure under section 27 of the Act to comply with (a) a work search
-- requirement under section 17(1)(a) (to take all reasonable action to obtain paid work etc.), or (b) a work availability requirement
-- under section 18(1).
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1637 | 103 Medium-level sanction
-- src:1638 | (1) This regulation specifies the reduction period for a sanctionable failure under section 27 of the Act (other sanctions) where it is a failure by the claimant to comply with—
-- src:1639 | (a) a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a) (to take all reasonable action to obtain paid work etc.); or
-- src:1640 | (b) a work availability requirement under section 18(1).
-- src:1641 | (2) The reduction in the circumstances described in the first column of the following table is the period set out in—
-- src:1642 | (a) the second column, where the claimant is aged 18 or over on the date of the sanctionable failure;
-- src:1643 | (b) the third column, where the claimant is aged 16 or 17 on the date of the sanctionable failure.
-- src:1644 | | Circumstances in which reduction period applies | Reduction period where claimant aged 18 or over | Reduction period where claimant aged 16 or 17 |
-- src:1645 | | Where there has been no previous sanctionable failure by the claimant that falls within paragraph (1) | 28 days | 7 days |
-- src:1646 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant that fall within paragraph (1) and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is not within 365 days beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure | 28 days | 7 days |
-- src:1647 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant that fall within paragraph (1) and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is within 365 days, but not within 14 days, beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure and the reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure is— | | |
-- src:1648 | | (a) 7 days | – | 14 days |
-- src:1649 | | (b) 14 days | – | 14 days |
-- src:1650 | | (c) 28 days | 91 days | – |
-- src:1651 | | (d) 91 days | 91 days | – |
-- src:1652 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant that fall within paragraph (1) and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is within 14 days beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure and the reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure is— | | |
-- src:1653 | | (a) 7 days | – | 7 days |
-- src:1654 | | (b) 14 days | – | 14 days |
-- src:1655 | | (c) 28 days | 28 days | – |
-- src:1656 | | (d) 91 days | 91 days | – |
@ref reg 103(1) (src:1637-1640)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work availability requirement under section 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 103(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work availability requirement under section 18(1)` MEANS
    `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` AND (`the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a)` OR `the failure is a failure to comply with a work availability requirement under section 18(1)`)

-- The most recent previous failure that falls within paragraph (1).
@ref reg 103(2) (src:1645-1647)
GIVEN failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Previous sanctionable failure`
`reg 103(2) — the most recent previous sanctionable failure that falls within paragraph (1)` failures MEANS
    `reg 102(2) — the most recent of some previous sanctionable failures`
        (filter (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 103(1)`) failures)

-- Paragraph (2): the table. Second column for 18 or over; third for 16 or 17. "–" is NOTHING.
@ref reg 103(2) (src:1641-1656)
GIVEN band IS AN `Age band for a reduction period`
      recency IS A `Recency of the most recent previous sanctionable failure`
      `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 103(2) — the reduction period in the table` band recency `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` MEANS
    CONSIDER recency
    WHEN `no previous sanctionable failure` THEN `no previous failure, or one not within 365 days`
    WHEN `previous failure not within 365 days` THEN `no previous failure, or one not within 365 days`
    WHEN `previous failure within 365 days but not within 14 days` THEN `within 365 days but not within 14 days`
    WHEN `previous failure within 14 days` THEN `within 14 days`
    WHERE
        `no previous failure, or one not within 365 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER band
            WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN JUST 28
            WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN JUST 7
        `within 365 days but not within 14 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER band
            WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 91
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 91 THEN JUST 91
                     ELSE NOTHING
            WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 7 THEN JUST 14
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 14
                     ELSE NOTHING
        `within 14 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER band
            WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 28
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 91 THEN JUST 91
                     ELSE NOTHING
            WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN
                IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 7 THEN JUST 7
                ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 14
                     ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 103(2) (src:1641-1643)
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `date of the current sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 103(2) — the reduction period for a failure within paragraph (1)` age `date of the current sanctionable failure` failures MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — the age band of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` age
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST band THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — how recent the most recent previous sanctionable failure is` `date of the current sanctionable failure` `the previous failure that counts`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST recency THEN `reg 103(2) — the reduction period in the table` band recency `the period of the previous failure`
    WHERE
        `the previous failure that counts` MEANS `reg 103(2) — the most recent previous sanctionable failure that falls within paragraph (1)` failures
        `the period of the previous failure` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the previous failure that counts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST p THEN p's `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 104 — Low-level sanction`

-- Paragraph (1): this regulation specifies the reduction period for a failure under section 27 where (a) the claimant falls within
-- section 21 or 22 of the Act on the date of the failure, and (b) it is a failure to comply with (i) a work-focused interview requirement
-- under section 15(1), (ii) a work preparation requirement under section 16(1), (iii) a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b),
-- or (iv) a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4).
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1657 | 104 Low-level sanction
-- src:1658 | (1) This regulation specifies the reduction period for a sanctionable failure under section 27 of the Act (other sanctions) where —
-- src:1659 | (a) the claimant falls within section 21 (claimants subject to work preparation requirement) or 22 (claimants subject to all work-related requirements) of the Act on the date of that failure; and
-- src:1660 | (b) it is a failure to comply with—
-- src:1661 | (i) a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1),
-- src:1662 | (ii) a work preparation requirement under section 16(1),
-- src:1663 | (iii) a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b) (to take any particular action specified by the Secretary of State to obtain work etc.), or
-- src:1664 | (iv) a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4) (connected requirements: interviews and verification of compliance).
-- src:1665 | (2) Where the claimant is aged 18 or over on the date of the sanctionable failure, the reduction period is the total of—
-- src:1666 | (a) the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with—
-- src:1667 | (i) the day before the date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State,
-- src:1668 | (ii) the day before the date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act (claimant subject to no work-related requirements),
-- src:1669 | (iii) the day before the date on which the claimant is no longer required to take a particular action specified as a work preparation requirement by the Secretary of State under section 16, or
-- src:1670 | (iv) the date on which the award terminates (other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple),
-- src:1671 | whichever is soonest; and
-- src:1672 | (b) in the circumstances described in the first column of the following table, the number of days set out in the second column.
-- src:1673 | | Circumstances applicable to claimant’s case | Number of days |
-- src:1674 | | Where there has been no previous sanctionable failure by the claimant that falls within paragraph (1) | 7 days |
-- src:1675 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant that fall within paragraph (1) and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is not within 365 days beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure | 7 days |
-- src:1676 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant that fall within paragraph (1) and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is within 365 days, but not within 14 days, beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure and the reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure is— | |
-- src:1677 | | (a) 7 days | 14 days |
-- src:1678 | | (b) 14 days | 28 days |
-- src:1679 | | (c) 28 days | 28 days |
-- src:1680 | | Where there have been one or more previous sanctionable failures by the claimant that fall within paragraph (1) and the date of the most recent previous sanctionable failure is within 14 days beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure and the reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure is— | |
-- src:1681 | | (a) 7 days | 7 days |
-- src:1682 | | (b) 14 days | 14 days |
-- src:1683 | | (c) 28 days | 28 days. |
-- src:1684 | (3) Where the claimant is aged 16 or 17 years on the date of the sanctionable failure, the reduction period is—
-- src:1685 | (a) the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with—
-- src:1686 | (i) the day before the date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State,
-- src:1687 | (ii) the day before the date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act (claimant subject to no work-related requirements),
-- src:1688 | (iii) the day before the date on which the claimant is no longer required to take a particular action specified as a work preparation requirement by the Secretary of State under section 16, or
-- src:1689 | (iv) date on which the award terminates (other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple),
-- src:1690 | whichever is soonest; and
-- src:1691 | (b) if there was another sanctionable failure of a kind mentioned in paragraph (1) within 365 days, but not within 14 days, beginning with the date of the current sanctionable failure, 7 days.
@ref reg 104(1) (src:1657-1664)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      group IS A `Work-related group`
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work preparation requirement under section 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 104(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` group `the failure is a failure to comply with a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work preparation requirement under section 16(1)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4)` MEANS
    `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act`
    AND `within section 21 or 22 of the Act`
    AND `one of the four kinds`
    WHERE
        `within section 21 or 22 of the Act` MEANS
            CONSIDER group
            WHEN `subject to no work-related requirements` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `subject to work-focused interview requirement only` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `subject to work-preparation requirement` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `subject to all work-related requirements` THEN TRUE
        `one of the four kinds` MEANS
            `the failure is a failure to comply with a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1)`
            OR `the failure is a failure to comply with a work preparation requirement under section 16(1)`
            OR `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b)`
            OR `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4)`

-- The days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever of four events is soonest (paragraphs (2)(a) and
-- (3)(a), and regulation 105(2) with three of them): (i) the day before the date the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the
-- Secretary of State; (ii) the day before the date the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act; (iii) the day before the date the
-- claimant is no longer required to take a particular action specified as a work preparation requirement; (iv) the date on which the award
-- terminates (other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple). Counting both ends, a period that ends
-- on the day before a date D has D minus the failure date days, and one that ends on D has one more. An event with no date yet is
-- left out; if none has a date the period has not been fixed, and the answer is NOTHING.
@ref reg 104(2)(a) (src:1665-1671)
@ref reg 104(3)(a) (src:1684-1690)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      b IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(2)(a) — the smaller of two numbers of days, whichever has one` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (minimum (LIST x, y))

@ref reg 104(2)(a) (src:1666-1670)
GIVEN `date of the sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `date of the event` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(2)(a) — the days up to the day before the date of an event` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date of the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of the event`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (Day d MINUS Day `date of the sanctionable failure`)

@ref reg 104(2)(a)(iv) (src:1670)
GIVEN `date of the sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `date on which the award terminates` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(2)(a)(iv) — the days up to the date on which the award terminates` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the award terminates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date on which the award terminates`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST ((Day d MINUS Day `date of the sanctionable failure`) PLUS 1)

-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
@ref reg 104(2)(a) (src:1665-1671)
GIVEN `date of the sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the claimant is no longer required to take a particular action specified as a work preparation requirement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the award terminates, other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(2)(a) — the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State` `date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act` `date on which the claimant is no longer required to take a particular action specified as a work preparation requirement` `date on which the award terminates, other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple` MEANS
    `reg 104(2)(a) — the smaller of two numbers of days, whichever has one`
        (`reg 104(2)(a) — the smaller of two numbers of days, whichever has one`
            (`reg 104(2)(a) — the days up to the day before the date of an event` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State`)
            (`reg 104(2)(a) — the days up to the day before the date of an event` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act`))
        (`reg 104(2)(a) — the smaller of two numbers of days, whichever has one`
            (`reg 104(2)(a) — the days up to the day before the date of an event` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant is no longer required to take a particular action specified as a work preparation requirement`)
            (`reg 104(2)(a)(iv) — the days up to the date on which the award terminates` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the award terminates, other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple`))

-- The most recent previous failure that falls within paragraph (1).
@ref reg 104(2)(b) (src:1674-1676)
GIVEN failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Previous sanctionable failure`
`reg 104(2)(b) — the most recent previous sanctionable failure that falls within paragraph (1)` failures MEANS
    `reg 102(2) — the most recent of some previous sanctionable failures`
        (filter (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)`) failures)

-- Paragraph (2)(b): the number of days in the table, for a claimant aged 18 or over.
@ref reg 104(2)(b) (src:1672-1683)
GIVEN recency IS A `Recency of the most recent previous sanctionable failure`
      `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(2)(b) — the number of days in the table` recency `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` MEANS
    CONSIDER recency
    WHEN `no previous sanctionable failure` THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `previous failure not within 365 days` THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `previous failure within 365 days but not within 14 days` THEN
        IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 7 THEN JUST 14
        ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 28
             ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 28
                  ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `previous failure within 14 days` THEN
        IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 7 THEN JUST 7
        ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 14
             ELSE IF `reduction period applicable to the most recent previous sanctionable failure` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 28
                  ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (2): where the claimant is aged 18 or over on the date of the failure, the reduction period is the total of (a) and (b).
@ref reg 104(2) (src:1665)
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `date of the current sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `the days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(2) — the reduction period of a claimant aged 18 or over` age `date of the current sanctionable failure` `the days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` failures MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — the age band of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` age
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST band THEN
        CONSIDER band
        WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN `the total of (a) and (b)`
    WHERE
        `the total of (a) and (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST a THEN
                CONSIDER `the number of days from the table`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (a PLUS b)
        `the number of days from the table` MEANS
            CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — how recent the most recent previous sanctionable failure is` `date of the current sanctionable failure` `the previous failure that counts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST recency THEN `reg 104(2)(b) — the number of days in the table` recency `the period of the previous failure`
        `the previous failure that counts` MEANS `reg 104(2)(b) — the most recent previous sanctionable failure that falls within paragraph (1)` failures
        `the period of the previous failure` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the previous failure that counts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST p THEN p's `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days`

-- Paragraph (3)(b): if there was another sanctionable failure of a kind mentioned in paragraph (1) within 365 days, but not within 14 days,
-- beginning with the date of the current failure, 7 days. Any such earlier failure counts, not only the most recent (fork F-104-1), read
-- backward as in fork F-102-1: a gap of 14 to 364 days. When there is none, this limb adds nothing: 0 days (fork F-104-2).
@ref reg 104(3)(b) (src:1691)
GIVEN `date of the current sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 104(3)(b) — the days for another failure within 365 days but not within 14 days` `date of the current sanctionable failure` failures MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN f YIELD (f's `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)`) AND ((Day `date of the current sanctionable failure` MINUS Day (f's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) AT LEAST 14) AND ((Day `date of the current sanctionable failure` MINUS Day (f's `date of the previous sanctionable failure`)) AT MOST 364)) failures
    THEN 7
    ELSE 0

-- Paragraph (3): where the claimant is aged 16 or 17 on the date of the failure, the reduction period is (a) the days ending with the
-- soonest event, and (b) 7 more if paragraph (3)(b) applies.
@ref reg 104(3) (src:1684)
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      `date of the current sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `the days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      failures IS A LIST OF `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 104(3) — the reduction period of a claimant aged 16 or 17` age `date of the current sanctionable failure` `the days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` failures MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — the age band of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` age
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST band THEN
        CONSIDER band
        WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN
            CONSIDER `the days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (a PLUS `reg 104(3)(b) — the days for another failure within 365 days but not within 14 days` `date of the current sanctionable failure` failures)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 105 — Lowest-level sanction`

-- Paragraph (1): this regulation specifies the reduction period for a failure under section 27 by a claimant who falls within section 20 of
-- the Act (work-focused interview requirement only) to comply with a requirement under that section.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
-- src:1692 | 105 Lowest-level sanction
-- src:1693 | (1) This regulation specifies the reduction period for a sanctionable failure under section 27 of the Act (other sanctions) where it is a failure by a claimant who falls within section 20 of the Act (claimants subject to work-focused interview requirement only) to comply with a requirement under that section.
-- src:1694 | (2) The reduction period is the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with—
-- src:1695 | (a) the day before the date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State;
-- src:1696 | (b) the day before the date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act (claimant subject to no work-related requirements); or
-- src:1697 | (c) the day on which the award terminates (other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple),
-- src:1698 | whichever is soonest.
@ref reg 105(1) (src:1692-1693)
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      group IS A `Work-related group`
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 20 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 105(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` group `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 20 of the Act` MEANS
    `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act`
    AND `within section 20 of the Act`
    AND `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 20 of the Act`
    WHERE
        `within section 20 of the Act` MEANS
            CONSIDER group
            WHEN `subject to no work-related requirements` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `subject to work-focused interview requirement only` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `subject to work-preparation requirement` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `subject to all work-related requirements` THEN FALSE

-- Paragraph (2): the days beginning with the date of the failure and ending with whichever is soonest of (a) the day before the claimant
-- meets a compliance condition, (b) the day before the claimant falls within section 19, (c) the day on which the award terminates
-- (other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple).
-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
@ref reg 105(2) (src:1694-1698)
GIVEN `date of the sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the award terminates, other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 105(2) — the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State` `date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act` `date on which the award terminates, other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple` MEANS
    `reg 104(2)(a) — the smaller of two numbers of days, whichever has one`
        (`reg 104(2)(a) — the days up to the day before the date of an event` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant meets a compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State`)
        (`reg 104(2)(a) — the smaller of two numbers of days, whichever has one`
            (`reg 104(2)(a) — the days up to the day before the date of an event` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act`)
            (`reg 104(2)(a)(iv) — the days up to the date on which the award terminates` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date on which the award terminates, other than by reason of the claimant ceasing to be, or becoming, a member of a couple`))
